"<div><div class=\" response-message\"></div></div><h2>Loot &amp; Reward System Design</h2>\n<p>✅ Design complete</p>\n<p>This loot and reward system is designed for <strong>Galactic Trader</strong>, a strategy game where progression is linear and driven by resource management and crafting. Since &quot;Trading&quot; is disabled in the traditional sense, the &quot;Trader&quot; aspect focuses on <strong>optimizing supply chains and converting loot into high-value ship components.</strong></p>\n<hr />\n<h3>1. Loot Tables by Content Type</h3>\n<h4>A. Common Activities (Asteroid Mining, Scout Skirmishes)</h4>\n<p><em>Focus: High-volume, low-value materials for base crafting and fuel.</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Item Types &amp; Rarities:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Star-Iron Ore (Common):</strong> 70% weight.</li>\n<li><strong>Plasma Trace (Common):</strong> 20% weight.</li>\n<li><strong>Basic Circuitry (Rare):</strong> 8% weight.</li>\n<li><strong>Data Fragment (Rare):</strong> 2% weight.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Scaling:</strong> Yield increases by 15% per Sector Level.</li>\n<li><strong>Pity System:</strong> &quot;Scrap Guarantee&quot; – Every 10th common activity without a Rare drop guarantees 2x Basic Circuitry.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>B. Elite Enemies (Pirate Captains, Rogue Drones)</h4>\n<p><em>Focus: Specialized components required for mid-tier upgrades.</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Item Types &amp; Rarities:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Refined Star-Iron (Common):</strong> 50% weight.</li>\n<li><strong>Plasma Cells (Rare):</strong> 35% weight.</li>\n<li><strong>Encrypted Data Shard (Rare):</strong> 10% weight.</li>\n<li><strong>Prototype Weapon Frame (Epic):</strong> 5% weight.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Scaling:</strong> Elites gain &quot;Affixes&quot; at higher levels; each Affix adds a 5% chance to roll the Epic table twice.</li>\n<li><strong>Pity System:</strong> &quot;Data Recovery&quot; – If no Data Shard drops in 5 Elite kills, the next one is guaranteed.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>C. Boss Encounters (Sector Overlords, Ancient Guardians)</h4>\n<p><em>Focus: Major progression leaps and unique crafting blueprints.</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Item Types &amp; Rarities:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Bulk Plasma/Iron Bundles (Rare):</strong> 100% (Guaranteed base).</li>\n<li><strong>Advanced Tech Core (Epic):</strong> 80% weight.</li>\n<li><strong>Ancient Artifact (Legendary):</strong> 15% weight.</li>\n<li><strong>Unique Ship Blueprint (Legendary):</strong> 5% weight.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Scaling:</strong> Bosses drop &quot;Sector Tokens&quot; used to bypass crafting timers in the current sector.</li>\n<li><strong>Pity System:</strong> &quot;The Blueprint Mercy&quot; – If a Legendary Blueprint hasn't dropped in 3 Boss kills, the 4th kill allows the player to choose one of three random Legendary Blueprints.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>D. Quest Rewards (Main Story &amp; Side Contracts)</h4>\n<p><em>Focus: Controlled progression and narrative milestones.</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Item Types &amp; Rarities:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Credits (Currency):</strong> Fixed amount based on difficulty.</li>\n<li><strong>Data Shards (Experience):</strong> Fixed amount.</li>\n<li><strong>Crafting Kits (Rare/Epic):</strong> Contains all materials needed for the next linear upgrade.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Scaling:</strong> Rewards are pegged to the player’s current &quot;Tech Tier&quot; to ensure they are always relevant.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>E. Achievement Rewards (Milestones &amp; Feats)</h4>\n<p><em>Focus: Long-term goals and &quot;Premium&quot; feel.</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Item Types &amp; Rarities:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Cosmetic Hull Liveries (Epic):</strong> 100% (Fixed).</li>\n<li><strong>Permanent Efficiency Buffs (Legendary):</strong> e.g., &quot;+5% Plasma Extraction.&quot;</li>\n<li><strong>Massive Credit Injections:</strong> To clear progression bottlenecks.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h3>2. Reward Structures</h3>\n<h4>Quest Completion</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Main Quests:</strong> Provide &quot;Key Components.&quot; These are non-random items required to unlock the next Sector. This prevents players from getting stuck due to bad RNG.</li>\n<li><strong>Side Contracts:</strong> Provide &quot;Resource Packs.&quot; Players can choose between an &quot;Iron Pack,&quot; &quot;Energy Pack,&quot; or &quot;Data Pack&quot; upon completion, allowing them to fill specific gaps in their economy.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Achievement Unlocks</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Tiered Achievements:</strong> (e.g., Mine 1k/10k/100k Iron).</li>\n<li><strong>Rewards:</strong> Each tier grants a &quot;Production Multiplier.&quot;\n<ul>\n<li><em>Bronze:</em> +2% yield.</li>\n<li><em>Silver:</em> +5% yield.</li>\n<li><em>Gold:</em> A &quot;Mastery Part&quot; used to craft the highest-tier gear.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Milestone Rewards (Linear Progression)</h4>\n<p>As the player reaches specific &quot;Net Worth&quot; or &quot;Tech Level&quot; milestones:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Level 5:</strong> Unlock &quot;Auto-Collector&quot; (Reduces manual clicking).</li>\n<li><strong>Level 10:</strong> Unlock &quot;Refinery&quot; (Converts Common resources to Rare at a 10:1 ratio).</li>\n<li><strong>Level 20:</strong> Unlock &quot;Jump Drive&quot; (Access to higher-tier loot tables).</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>First-Time Bonuses</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>First Elite Kill:</strong> Guaranteed Epic Weapon Frame to give a power spike.</li>\n<li><strong>First Sector Clear:</strong> Large cache of Data Shards to jumpstart the next tier's research.</li>\n<li><strong>First Craft:</strong> Refund of 50% of materials spent to encourage experimentation with the crafting system.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h3>3. System Mechanics &amp; Balance</h3>\n<h4>Scaling with Difficulty</h4>\n<p>To prevent early-game items from becoming obsolete, <strong>Galactic Trader</strong> uses a <strong>&quot;Component Upcycling&quot;</strong> logic.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Loot from Sector 1 (Star-Iron) can be compressed into &quot;High-Tensile Plates&quot; needed for Sector 3.</li>\n<li>This ensures that even if a player returns to a low-level area, the loot still contributes to their high-level goals.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Anti-Frustration Features (Bad Luck Protection)</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The &quot;Entropy&quot; Meter:</strong> A hidden counter for every rarity. Every time a loot roll fails to hit a Rare/Epic/Legendary, the probability for the next roll increases by a fixed percentage (e.g., +1% for Rare, +0.5% for Epic). This resets upon a successful drop.</li>\n<li><strong>Resource Transmutation:</strong> If a player has an excess of one resource but zero of another due to RNG, the &quot;Black Market&quot; (a menu-based sink) allows them to exchange resources at a 4:1 ratio.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Value Proposition</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Short-term:</strong> Common loot provides the &quot;fuel&quot; to keep playing (Plasma) and basic repairs (Iron).</li>\n<li><strong>Long-term:</strong> Epic and Legendary drops are the only way to increase &quot;Cargo Capacity&quot; and &quot;Jump Range,&quot; which are the primary gates for linear progression.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Summary of Loot Flow</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Acquire:</strong> Kill/Mine (RNG-based loot).</li>\n<li><strong>Stabilize:</strong> Quests/Milestones (Fixed-reward injections).</li>\n<li><strong>Refine:</strong> Crafting (Convert low-tier loot to high-tier gear).</li>\n<li><strong>Progress:</strong> Use gear to reach the next Sector with better loot tables.</li>\n</ol>\n<div><div class=\" completion-message response-message\"></div></div>"